<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hiempsal II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 60 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hiempsal II was king of Numidia from about 88 BCE until around 60 BCE, a son of King Gauda and the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juba-i">Juba I</a>. Driven out by the Marian faction during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s civil wars, he was restored by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> in 81 BCE and ruled thereafter as a loyal Roman client. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sallust">Sallust</a> drew on Punic books said to belong to a King Hiempsal, probably him, for his account of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hiempsal-ii.jpg" alt="Hiempsal II" width="320" height="164" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hiempsal_II_coin_with_reverse.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
